<p dir=3D"auto">I wanted to use these boards to create some low power BTHom=
e sensors. I have boards from many different sources. Some exhibit great po=
wer consumption, only 4 uA in sleep, with EXTVCC disabled. Others had a con=
sumption of 60 uA, which is still pretty good but it's 15x more. After some=
 component swapping, I found the problem to be the W5 marked diode. This is=
 supposed to be a BAT60B Schottky diode, with a voltage drop of 0.24 V. On =
the high power consumption boards I instead measured a drop of 0.7 V, indic=
ating a regular silicon diode. What's more concerning is that apparently th=
e reverse leakage current of this diode was also much worse and this is wha=
t was causing the power consumption.</p>
